WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.709
People can't get enough of the Clown Prince
of Crime.

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:06.730
At least, that's what Warner Brothers seems
to think, now that news has emerged that not

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.010
one, but two solo movies for the character
are being developed.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.159
It's a move that raises a lot of questions
for the casual moviegoer.

00:00:13.159 --> 00:00:16.880
Is Jared Leto still the Joker, or are we getting
Joaquin Phoenix?

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.580
And if they're both the Joker, how?

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.330
We've got the answers to all of this and more,
so if you're wondering why everything seems

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.700
to be coming up Joker, stay with us.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.930
Developing DC

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.890
Warner Brothers' DC Extended Universe is a
movie series that's hard to talk about without

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.960
bringing up comparisons to Marvel.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.750
Launched in 2013 with Man of Steel, the DCEU
is a direct response to the success that Marvel

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.890
Studios and Disney have been having with their
cinematic universe since the release of Iron

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.720
Man in 2008.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.640
Big differences have emerged in the way we
learn about upcoming movies in each franchise.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.700
Regarding Marvel, we generally don't know
what they're working on until they officially

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.540
announce something, meaning that by the time
we hear about a movie that they're doing,

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.090
we can be fairly confident it's actually going
to happen.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:06.010
DC takes the opposite approach, with leaks
and rumors emerging about a downright confusing

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.900
number of movies in development, some of which
will more than likely never see the light

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.900
of day.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.190
It's almost too much to keep track of, making
things extra confusing for the casual fan.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:19.410
"Cuz there's been talk of like, the Harley-Joker
film, and the Gotham City Sirens.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.810
Are those two distinct things, are you talking
about the Sirens project?"

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.390
"No, it's a totally separate one."

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:24.710
"Oh my god."

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.490
The joke book

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.510
Let's talk about the DC movies just related
to the Joker, in order of how likely they

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:32.979
seem to actually happen.

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:38.170
First off, there's Suicide Squad 2, which
is reportedly set to feature Jared Leto returning

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.470
to the role as part of an ensemble.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:46.070
Next, there's the most-recently announced
Joker solo movie, also set to center on Leto's

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.070
Joker.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:52.119
Then there's the biggest wild card of all:
the Martin Scorsese-produced, Todd Phillips-directed,

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:55.200
Joaquin Phoenix-led Joker origin movie.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.520
Finally, there's the "twisted romantic comedy"
project featuring Harley Quinn and the Joker.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.260
Supposedly, this movie replaces the Gotham
City Sirens movie we've heard so many reports

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:09.649
about, which also was reportedly going to
involve Leto's Joker.

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:13.840
In other words, Warner Brothers could currently
be working on no less than four different

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.930
films involving the Joker, two of them solo
movies with completely different actors.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.900
The obvious question is how the Joaquin Phoenix
movie could possibly fit in with the tone

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.340
established by Leto's Joker, much less the
continuity of the DCEU.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.500
The answer is simple: It won't.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.560
Elseworlds

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.150
Even before Justice League saw a theatrical
release, word was out that Warner Brothers

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.670
was in the process of re-evaluating its strategy
regarding DC Comics movies.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.920
Specifically, the studio started exploring
the possibility that this whole shared universe

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.720
thing might not be all it's cracked up to
be.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.959
They'd hardly be the only ones to screw up
a movie mega-verse.

00:02:51.959 --> 00:03:00.680
[Yelling and crashing]

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.810
Word is, Warner Brothers is in the process
of creating a new banner for movies to take

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.950
place outside of shared universe continuity.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:12.620
Under this arrangement, multiple actors will
be able to play the same role, with anything

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:16.440
that happens outside the shared universe being
irrelevant to it.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.110
That way, any actor will be able to play the
Joker on the big screen in an alternate-universe

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:25.090
story, having no effect on the storyline of
Jared Leto's Joker.

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:28.810
It works for DC's animated universe, so why
not the big screen?

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:33.690
For now, this separate banner remains untitled,
and Warner Brothers hasn't done a whole lot

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.580
to make the general public aware that they're
making this move, leaving the door open for

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:41.209
what feels like an unnecessary amount of confusion.

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:42.239
Jokin' Phoenix

00:03:42.239 --> 00:03:47.550
So, what is this alternate-universe, Elseworlds-style
Joker movie?

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.010
Here's what we know right now.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:55.220
According to reports, DC is developing a solo
Joker origin story starring Joaquin Phoenix,

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.180
directed by Todd Phillips of The Hangover
series fame.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.390
Phillips is co-writing the script with Scott
Silver, who wrote 8 Mile and The Fighter.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:06.580
The movie is being produced in part by Martin
Scorsese, and at this point, there's every

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.000
indication that Phoenix really has signed
on for the role, though he's publicly been

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.099
cagey about his involvement so far.

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:19.180
A lot of the information that we have about
this movie's premise comes from MMA fighter-turned-comedian

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:24.360
Brendan Schaub, who spilled some showbiz gossip
during an appearance on the Joe Rogan Experience

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.360
podcast.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.809
"As a kid, he had like a permanent smile and
everyone made fun of him.

00:04:28.809 --> 00:04:30.129
It's like on the streets of Brooklyn.

00:04:30.129 --> 00:04:32.139
It's like super dark and real.

00:04:32.139 --> 00:04:33.210
I can't wait."

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.009
Joker: A Joker Story

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:39.400
Right now, not much is known about Jared Leto's
Joker movie.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:43.289
The hunt is currently on for a director and
a screenwriter, and it's unknown whether the

00:04:43.289 --> 00:04:46.960
movie will be produced before or after Suicide
Squad 2.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.919
Either way, the earliest we'll see this is
in 2019.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:51.919
As for the plot?

00:04:51.919 --> 00:04:54.680
Well, it probably won't be an origin story.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:58.580
Leto going forward with the movie would seem
to indicate that any bad blood that may have

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:02.339
existed between him and Warner Brothers has
more or less dissolved.

00:05:02.339 --> 00:05:07.389
If you'll recall, Leto seemed pretty peeved
at the way his Suicide Squad work was treated

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:11.789
in the editing room, with most of his involved
performance ending up on the cutting room

00:05:11.789 --> 00:05:13.319
floor.

00:05:13.319 --> 00:05:14.559
Elseworlds apart

00:05:14.559 --> 00:05:19.300
If the Elseworlds-style banner takes off,
there are many stories in DC's stable that

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.039
might get adaptations.

00:05:21.039 --> 00:05:26.111
One potential project Warner Brothers was
once considering is Superman: Red Son, a story

00:05:26.111 --> 00:05:30.439
that imagines how things might have shaken
out had the Kryptonian crash-landed in the

00:05:30.439 --> 00:05:31.949
USSR.

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:37.800
As a story, it's the perfect example of what
this alternate world movie banner could accomplish.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.289
Making multiple Joker films may sound like
the strangest way to start it, but if Warner

00:05:42.289 --> 00:05:46.509
Brothers hits on something, it could very
well revolutionize the way studios approach

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:48.060
comic book movies.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:52.229
Maybe it's time to go to the next level, and
wouldn't it be funny if DC was the one who

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:53.379
leads us there?

00:05:53.379 --> 00:05:57.639
Despite the mistakes of even the rather recent
past, it could work out for everyone.

00:05:57.639 --> 00:05:59.349
And that's no joke.

00:05:59.349 --> 00:06:00.789
Thanks for watching!

00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:03.439
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:03.439 --> 00:06:05.539
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

